@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] card-sheet-pages-stay-in-the-sheet
A card action that opens a child page MUST keep the same sheet window, panel and drag
state. The page content and heading change without restarting the sheet. At the
normal detent the panel MAY resize to the new content through the page transition;
at the tall detent the grabber and header MUST stay at the same height.
The root's cross becomes Back;
the header's Back and the phone's Back return to the parent without dismissing the
sheet. The phone's Back dismisses only from the root page. Each page MUST retain its
own scroll position when another page is shown.
Source: pulls.review `kit-sheet-pages-stay-in-the-sheet`, DESIGN rules 78 and 115,
at ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; see `docs/pully-ui-reference.md`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;reliability] card-space-creation-outlives-its-page
Leaving the New space form or dismissing the sheet MUST NOT cancel an accepted
Create and add: the space is still made, the card is still added to it, and the
spaces are refreshed. A pending creation MUST remain guarded against duplicate
submission when the form is reopened. Completion MUST close the form only if it is
still showing.
Source: the same-sheet creation flow and its native Back/dismissal regressions,
22 October 2026; Create and add follows Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader
prototype, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] card-sheet-pages-follow-navigation
Opening a child page MUST move it in from the right and move the parent left; Back
MUST reverse that direction. Page content travels through the Pully blurred slide,
and the grabber and header controls MUST NOT travel sideways with it. When the
system disables animations, navigation MUST finish without the slide or blur.
Source: pulls.review DESIGN rules 78 and 105, `PagedSheetPanel` and `BlurSwitch`,
at ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; see `docs/pully-ui-reference.md`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] card-sheet-header-stays-clear
A card sheet MUST have one header above its scrolling content. The leading close
or Back control MUST remain separate from the title and have a 44dp target. Content
scrolling under the header MUST fade through the sheet's paper, leaving the title
and controls sharp and unobstructed.
Source: pulls.review `kit-sheet-header-is-fixed`, DESIGN rules 70, 74 and 77,
at ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; see `docs/pully-ui-reference.md`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] new-space-is-made-in-place
All spaces, titled Add to space, MUST offer New space in place: a form on the same
page with the space's name, its colour and Create and add, open at once when there
are no spaces yet. Create and add MUST make the space and add the card to it. A
failed creation MUST keep the form and its name for retry. Header Back and Android
Back return to Choose one, then dismiss.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026 (M10, new space
inline), which replaces the 22 October child creation page that did not add the
card.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] add-to-space-sits-in-choose-one
Choose one MUST show Add to space in place: up to three spaces as small mosaics of
their cards, the suggested space first with a Suggested badge, then the card's own
spaces, then the rest, each adding or removing the card with one tap, and All
spaces. The suggestion is the space holding the most other cards that share a tag
or a site with this card, and never one the card is already in. All spaces lists
the suggestion, then every space with its mosaic and card count; holding a space
MUST show its latest cards until it is let go.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026 (M12, hold to
look inside; M13, suggested space first).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] card-delete-is-held-then-undone
Delete card MUST be held for 1.3 seconds, filling as it goes; letting go sooner
keeps the card. While it is held the page behind the sheet MUST shrink and fade
with the hold, unless the system disables animations. Once the hold completes the
sheet and reader close and a bar with the card's name offers Undo for 5 seconds.
The card MUST NOT be trashed until Undo has run out, Undo MUST put it back where it
was, and a trash that fails MUST bring it back and show why. Accessibility services
delete with one action, since Undo covers a slip.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026 (H10, hold to
delete; M14, the card shrinks while Delete is held).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] card-sheet-actions-have-hierarchy
The root sheet, titled Choose one, MUST lead with the card's big choices (Add to
space, Same Vibe, Reader Mode) as raised cards with a muted line on what each
means, then its quick actions as tiles two by two (Open source, Copy, Download, Top
of Mind, Add tags), then Delete card alone in its own group, omitting what the card
cannot do. The Top of Mind tile MUST show an ink on state while the card is pinned.
Section headings MUST be small, muted and non-folding, without a count, divider or
chevron. Cards and tiles use 16dp corners and Pully's 2dp-down, 12dp-blur, 10% ink
canvas shadow with its tight edge; header controls use the 10dp/8% variant. The
title MUST remain centered in its own fixed area even while its animated content
changes. The grabber has a 14dp gap to the header; the first content respects
Pully's 20dp top gap.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026, for the
order; pulls.review DESIGN rules 45, 70, 74 and 141; SheetHeading, SheetCard,
QuickAction and SheetHeader at f651a784cfca9b3730c60116832b89bbe236c9c3;
Tavi's 22 October 2026 request to port the composition as well as sheet motion.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] card-sheet-accent-is-only-a-top-hint
A card sheet MUST keep neutral Pully paper, raised groups, controls and primary
actions. The selected card's accent MUST be limited to a faint wash fading out
within the top 64dp and the grabber. Child pages MUST retain that hint without
tinting the body or their fields. Semantic colors such as Delete and space
selection colors remain independent of the card-type accent.
Source: Tavi's explicit correction, 22 October 2026: "Don't paint the entire
bottom sheets in the color of the card type, just a little hint at the top of it".

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] card-share-sheet-offers-what-the-card-has
The reader's Share button MUST open a Share sheet in the card's sheet, titled Share,
offering only what the card has: The link for a card with a web link, The words for
a note or a post (a post's words carry its link), and Copy link. Each choice closes
the sheet before it hands off to the system's share sheet or the clipboard.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026.
